    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d600-a1">

                <pb facs="0815" n="701" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg701"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure—Translation]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Mexican Secretary of State for Foreign
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Pani</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the American Chargé</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Summerlin</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-10-21"><hi rendition="#italic">October 21,
                        1922</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Summerlin</hi>: I have the pleasure to
                    acknowledge receipt of your communication of the 19th instant.</p>
                <p>I know that very shortly there will be presented to Congress by the Executive
                    Power a definite proposal for the regulation of Article <pb facs="0816" n="702"
                        xml:id="pg702"/> 27 insofar as it relates to petroleum. As soon as this
                    takes place, in accordance with your wishes, I will have the pleasure of sending
                    you a copy of said proposed regulation.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. J. Pani</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
